Today I solved leetcode question 824:Goat Latin.

Description: We are given a sentence in english and we must convert it to goat latin.
              Rules of goat latin are:
              If a word begins with a vowel ('a', 'e', 'i', 'o', or 'u'), append "ma" to the end of the word.
                  eg- The word "apple" becomes "applema".
              If a word begins with a consonant (i.e., not a vowel), remove the first letter and append it to the end, then add "ma".
                  eg- The word "goat" becomes "oatgma".
              Add one letter 'a' to the end of each word per its word index in the sentence, starting with 1.
                   eg- The first word gets "a" added to the end, the second word gets "aa" added to the end, and so on.

Solution:  First we create 3 variables, answer, location and i.
            Location and i will be zero and answer will be an empty string.
            So we start our while loop till the end of our sentence.
            We will again run a while loop till there are empty spaces at location i.
            Then we will create a word variable.
            Here we will increase location by 1.
            Now we will push all letters in word till we either reach end of sentence or till we reach an empty space.
            Then we will check if first letter of the word is a vowel or constant.
            If it is a vowel then we will add ma to our word and add it to answer. And we will also add same a as the location of current word.
            Then we will check if i is at the end of sentence or not. If not we will add an empty space to answer.
            If it is not a vowel then we will first create a new variable named neww_word which will be an empty string.
            Here we will add all the letters of word except its first letter which we will add at last.
            We will then add ma and a's same as loaction amount.
            Then we will check if i is at the end of sentence or not. If not we will add an empty space to answer.
